ia Independent System Operator. It is intended to be used as an aid in cross-referencing different datasets.  It is not always possible to map codes across the various datasets. There are instances where plants codes can have a \"one-to-many\" or \"many-to-many\" match thereby presenting difficulties in presenting a tabular list.  Additionally, plants outside of the CA-ISO balancing authority area will not have a Resource ID assigned as there is no need for the CA-ISO to track plants outside of their balancing area. \r\n\r\nThis list may have errors and other incomplete data. \r\n\r\nThis list is subject to change without notice.\r\n\r\nFile Listing Date: May 5, 2016", "format": "XLS", "hash": "", "id": "da9c6a60-c510-481d-a335-444108165064", "last_modified": null, "metadata_modified": "2026-09-30T19:07:27.894200", "mimetype": null, "mimetype_inner": null, "name": "Energy Commission Power Plant ID Cross Reference Table", "package_id": "08a20692-ad33-4556-8b0b-4db153124688", "position": 3, "resource_type": null, "size": null, "state": "active", "url": "http://www.energy.ca.gov/almanac/electricity_data/web_qfer/Energy_Commission_Power_Plant_ID_Cross_Reference_Table.xls", "url_type": null}, {"cache_last_updated": null, "cache_url": null, "created": "2026-09-30T19:07:27.953232", "datastore_active": false, "description": "Heat Rate: The heat rate as expressed in MMBtu/MWh. A more common reference for heat rates is typically Btu/kWh: simply multiply the given heat rate by 1,000 to convert from MMBtu/MWh to Btu/kWh.", "format": "HTML", "hash": "", "id": "7b8e4e0f-e9be-4a20-9b7a-409bae463065", "last_modified": null, "metadata_modified": "2026-09-30T19:07:27.896787", "mimetype": null, "mimetype_inner": null, "name": "Heat Rates", "package_id": "08a20692-ad33-4556-8b0b-4db153124688", "position": 4, "resource_type": null, "size": null, "state": "active", "url": "https://ww2.energy.ca.gov/almanac/electricity_data/web_qfer/Heat_Rates_cms.php", "url_type": null}, {"cache_last_upd